{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Infobox UK constituency |name = Nottingham North and Kimberley |parliament = uk |image = {{maplink|frame=yes|frame-align=center|plain=yes|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Nottingham North and Kimberley (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame-height=200|frame-width=250}} |caption = Boundaries since 2024 |image2 = [[File:East Midlands - Nottingham North and Kimberley constituency.svg|175px|alt=Map of constituency]] |caption2 = Boundary of Nottingham North and Kimberley in the East Midlands |year = 2024 |abolished = |type = County |elects_howmany = One |previous = [[Nottingham North (UK Parliament constituency)|Nottingham North]] |next = |electorate = 74,515 (2023)<ref>{{cite web |url= https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition-east-midlands/#lg_nottingham-north-and-kimberley-bc-74515 |title= The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume two: Constituency names, designations and composition – East Midlands |publisher=Boundary Commission for England |access-date=3 July 2024 |df=dmy }}</ref> |mp = [[To be confirmed|TBC]] |party = [[To be confirmed|TBC]] |region = England |county = [[Nottinghamshire]] |towns = [[Bulwell]], [[Kimberley, Nottinghamshire|Kimberley]] }} '''Nottingham North and Kimberley''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – East Midlands {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-east-midlands/ |access-date=2023-07-14 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> It will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].
== Boundaries == Further to the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], which came into effect for the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]], the composition of the constituency is as follows (as they existed on 1 December 2020):
* The Borough of Broxtowe wards of: Kimberley; Nuthall East & Strelley; Watnall & Nuthall West.
* The City of Nottingham wards of: Aspley; Basford; Bestwood; Bulwell; Bulwell Forest; Leen Valley.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule I Part I}}</ref>
It includes the following areas:
* The former [[Nottingham North (UK Parliament constituency)|Nottingham North]] constituency, excluding the Bilborough ward (now to be included in [[Nottingham South (UK Parliament constituency)|Nottingham South]]) * The Leen Valley ward, transferred from [[Nottingham South (UK Parliament constituency)|Nottingham South]] * The communities of [[Kimberley, Nottinghamshire|Kimberley]] and [[Nuthall]], currently part of the [[Broxtowe (UK Parliament constituency)|Broxtowe]] constituency.
